.TH "CANDY\-CODE" 1 "" "candy\-code" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
candy\-code \- An agentic coding assistant.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B candy\-code
[options] <command>
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR...
Print more detail
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR...
Attach a tag
.SH "MODEL"
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL\fR
Model to use
.br
Environment: CANDY_CODE_MODEL.
.TP
\fB\-\-effort\fR \fIEFFORT\fR
Reasoning effort
.br
Default: low. Possible values: low, high.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcandy\-code run\fR [options] \-\-max\-turns <MAX_TURNS> <arg>
Run one prompt
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-turns\fR \fIMAX_TURNS\fR
Turn limit
.br
Required.
.RE
.TP
\fBcandy\-code config\fR [options] <command>
Read settings
.TP
\fBcandy\-code config get\fR [options] <arg>
Print one setting
.TP
\fBcandy\-code doctor\fR [options] [<arg>...]
Check the install's health
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CANDY_CODE_MODEL
Used for \-\-model of candy\-code when it is not given.
